  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Booz Allen Hamilton has obligated $108M in federal contracts in FY2027 to date. Booz Allen Hamilton received 79 awards so far this fiscal year with an average award size of $1.4M, and obligations fell 98.3% year over year. General Services Administration is the largest buyer of Booz Allen Hamilton this year, obligating $91M, followed by Department of Commerce with $9.2M and Department of Homeland Security with $3.7M. Computer Systems Design Services and Engineering Services are the top markets for Booz Allen Hamilton, with $35M and $30.5M respectively. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) accounts for $20.5M. Smaller markets include Custom Computer Programming Services at $35K and Research and Development in the Social Sciences and Humanities at $0. This fiscal-year snapshot is partial and reflects contract obligations rather than the full contract values for awards or expiring contracts.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How much has Booz Allen Hamilton received so far this fiscal year?",
        "body": "Booz Allen Hamilton has obligated $108M in FY2027 to date. Booz Allen Hamilton received 79 awards this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.4M. Booz Allen Hamilton obligations are down 98.3% versus the prior year period."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest federal buyers of Booz Allen Hamilton this year?",
        "body": "General Services Administration is the largest buyer of Booz Allen Hamilton this year, obligating $91M. Department of Commerce and Department of Homeland Security follow, obligating $9.2M and $3.7M respectively. National Aeronautics and Space Administration, Department of Veterans Affairs, and Department of Energy also bought services, obligating $2.2M, $1.8M, and $523K respectively."
      }
    ]
